Validate a defined prediction against independent physical evidence (@fd-validation: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @fluid-dynamics, #source "../sources/CFD-Verification-and-Validation-NPARC.lingua#r_7P72ZWZEJ0SVMWFDGK52N9AZPV", #source "../sources/Turbulence-Modeling-Resource.lingua#r_42VW512D9MG3Z0SBJ78N7DAPE6", #source "../sources/PIV-Uncertainty-Sciacchitano.lingua#r_4PHTCFRTAGSCNV1TK192VZHGQ6", #fluid-dynamics "A-reproducible-fluid-case-from-geometry-to-evidence.lingua#r_2PAK85R8DRMK4F04X4049NE49W") { r_6H9AXRJ7C8KS3CQKVAPK0BW0GV
**Read:** [CFD verification and validation — NPARC Alliance](../sources/CFD-Verification-and-Validation-NPARC.lingua#r_7P72ZWZEJ0SVMWFDGK52N9AZPV), validation process, uncertainty and applicability; [Turbulence Modeling Resource — model definitions and benchmarks](../sources/Turbulence-Modeling-Resource.lingua#r_42VW512D9MG3Z0SBJ78N7DAPE6), selected experimental validation case and its original report; [Uncertainty quantification in particle image velocimetry — Sciacchitano](../sources/PIV-Uncertainty-Sciacchitano.lingua#r_4PHTCFRTAGSCNV1TK192VZHGQ6), matching measurement and derived observables.

A validation comparison needs a specified physical quantity, conditions and intended use. Match the simulation's averaging and observation operator to the experiment: a pointwise instantaneous velocity is not directly comparable to a finite-window, spatially filtered mean. Retain measured boundary and property uncertainties as part of the comparison.

Use data not consumed in selecting or fitting the model whenever feasible. Compare several relevant observables and operating conditions, including a case likely to expose the model's limitations. Separate numerical error, sampling error, experimental uncertainty and model discrepancy before interpreting a mismatch.

State the domain in which the comparison supports a prediction and where extrapolation begins. A model can be adequate for total pressure loss and inadequate for a local peak stress or mixing rate. Preserve residual structure and failed cases; changing a closure after seeing validation data turns that data into development evidence and requires a new independent comparison.

**Continue:** [A reproducible fluid case from geometry to evidence](A-reproducible-fluid-case-from-geometry-to-evidence.lingua#r_2PAK85R8DRMK4F04X4049NE49W).

